      "message": "This is technically a different mask than the generic unpack loop, which masks to `0xF`, but we don\u0027t allow regular swizzles that go past `xyzw`, so it didn\u0027t make any difference either way; the inputs will always be in that range, and we always pack into 4-bit nybbles. (The SkRP \"shuffle\" op allows 16-wide shuffling, but that isn\u0027t exposed directly in SkSL anywhere; it\u0027s used to do things like matrix transposes.)",
